# Approved enrichment source domains (strict allow-list)
# =======================================================
#
# Rename this file to `approved_domains.txt` to ACTIVATE it.
#
# While `data/approved_domains.txt` exists, it overrides the category rules in
# app/sourcing.py entirely: only the domains listed here may be fetched, and
# everything else is rejected with a reason. That is the right configuration for
# a graded or audited run, where the source set should be agreed in advance
# rather than decided by whatever gets pasted into the box.
#
# While the file does NOT exist, the category policy applies instead
# (default `manufacturer_only`: marketplaces, distributors, encyclopedias and
# forums are rejected; unrecognised domains are permitted but flagged).
#
# One domain per line. Subdomains and www are handled automatically, so
# `turck.com` also permits `www.turck.com` and `pdb2.turck.de`.
# `#` starts a comment.

